<h1>Veinminer</h1>
<p><strong>Veinminer</strong> lets players break connected veins with one normal block break. It is designed to work immediately after install: hold Shift while mining a supported block and the vein is mined automatically.</p>
<p>No <code>/veinminer setup</code> command is required.</p>

<hr />

<h2>Key Features</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Out-of-box basic mining</strong> - install, hold Shift, and mine.</li>
  <li><strong>Server-side default flow</strong> - optional client keybind support is available but not required for Shift activation.</li>
  <li><strong>Connected vein scanning</strong> - mines supported ore/log veins with safe block limits.</li>
  <li><strong>Tool and block controls</strong> - server owners can manage allowed blocks and tools.</li>
  <li><strong>Durability safety</strong> - optional protection against breaking tools.</li>
  <li><strong>Optional advanced systems</strong> - particles, cooldown, hunger/exhaustion, LuckPerms integration, and test/admin tools.</li>
  <li><strong>Hidden advanced commands</strong> - advanced/admin commands are registered only when <code>advanced.enabled = true</code>.</li>
</ul>

<hr />

<h2>Basic Usage</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Install the correct Fabric or NeoForge jar.</li>
  <li>Start the game/server.</li>
  <li>Hold Shift while mining a supported ore/log block.</li>
  <li>Use <code>/veinminer toggle</code> only if you want to disable or re-enable the feature for yourself.</li>
</ol>
<p>Normal players do not need commands for the default mining flow, but per-user preferences are available under <code>/veinminer</code>.</p>

<hr />

<h2>Commands</h2>
<h3>Default commands</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Command</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>/veinminer</code></td><td>Show quick help.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>/veinminer help [topic]</code></td><td>Show help for <code>toggle</code>, <code>reload</code>, <code>activation</code>, <code>togglemessages</code>, or <code>particles</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>/veinminer toggle</code></td><td>Toggle Veinminer for yourself.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>/veinminer activation keybind</code></td><td>Toggle your activation input between Shift and the optional client keybind.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>/veinminer activation mode hold</code> / <code>toggle</code></td><td>Set your activation mode.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>/veinminer togglemessages &lt;permission|disabled|cooldown|durability&gt;</code></td><td>Toggle your own feedback messages.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>/veinminer particles toggle</code></td><td>Toggle your own outline particles.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>/veinminer particles setcolor &lt;red&gt; &lt;green&gt; &lt;blue&gt;</code></td><td>Set your own outline particle color.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>/veinminer particles setduration &lt;ticks&gt;</code></td><td>Set your own outline particle duration.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>/veinminer reload</code></td><td>Reload configs from disk. Requires admin/manage permission.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Admin commands</h3>
<p>Admin commands are always registered under <code>/vmadmin</code> and require admin/manage permission:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>/vmadmin blocks ...</code> - manage global block lists.</li>
  <li><code>/vmadmin tools ...</code> - manage allowed tools.</li>
  <li><code>/vmadmin settings ...</code> - manage block list mode, max blocks, cooldown, exhaustion, and LuckPerms settings.</li>
  <li><code>/vmadmin reload</code> - reload configs from disk.</li>
  <li><code>/vmadmin confirm</code> - confirm a pending destructive admin action.</li>
  <li><code>/vmadmin cancel</code> - cancel a pending destructive admin action.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Advanced commands</h3>
<p>Advanced commands are only registered when <code>advanced.enabled = true</code>:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>/vmadvanced blockpertool ...</code> - manage per-tool block lists.</li>
  <li><code>/vmadvanced settings blockpertool</code> - toggle per-tool block list mode.</li>
  <li><code>/vmadvanced test</code> - run the advanced feature test harness.</li>
</ul>

<hr />

<h2>Config</h2>
<p>Generated under <code>config/Veinminer/</code>:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>GeneralConfig.toml</code></li>
  <li><code>ToolsList.toml</code></li>
  <li><code>BlocksList.toml</code></li>
  <li><code>BlockPerToolList.toml</code></li>
</ul>

<h3>Important defaults</h3>
<pre><code>basic.enabled = true
basic.activation_key = "SHIFT"
basic.require_correct_tool = true
visual.show_particles = true
advanced.enabled = false
advanced.debug_logging = false
advanced.block_limits.max_blocks = 64</code></pre>

<hr />

<h2>Compatibility</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Fabric: Minecraft 1.20 through 1.21.11.</li>
  <li>NeoForge: Minecraft 1.21 through 1.21.11.</li>
  <li>Dedicated servers and single-player integrated servers.</li>
  <li>No Forge builds are currently planned.</li>
</ul>

<hr />

<h2>Client Optional</h2>
<p>Installing the client build enables the keybind and sends key state to the server. Default key: <strong>V</strong>.</p>
<p>Without the client, Shift/sneak activation remains available and is the default.</p>

